From 1104a89423b3ebf552db8e4419ffdaf1467cb6e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:11:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/23] fate: add ac4 decoder tests

framemd5/framecrc decode tests over the uploaded suite clips, plus
probe/copy/seek demux tests. Goldens recorded from the real decoder
(pinning current behavior; no independent-decoder anchor yet).
ims120 pins presentation 1 (default pres hits a v1-fatal mid-stream
config change in that clip; decoder is EXPERIMENTAL).

Fractional-spf pair over the pre-existing suite 29.97 fps clip
(fate-ac4-frac decode + fate-ac4-frac-copy demux) pins the exact
1601/1602 output counts and pts alternation. Encoder-layout
negatives (7.1, 5.1.4: exit 234 + message, AC4_ENCODER-guarded so
they stay empty until Series C lands) fold in the C08 gate script's
pins. fate-ac4-crc-bad is fate-ac4-skip-bad: the wrap performs no
CRC check, so the honest name pins skip-with-warning, not a reject.
seek-eof carries -copyts so the golden pins the demuxer's true +4096
clamp stamp instead of the CLI seek-offset -235904.
Mono + codec-4 gap tests stay deferred (no public bytes exist for either).

Signed-off-by: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
